These sensors are concentrated on the upper part of the human body, as most gestures involve upper-body movements. This strategic placement ensures accurate data collection for gesture recognition, focusing on areas with significant motion activity. As the subject performs gestures, the movement is captured by sensors placed on the body as well as devices positioned on the ground and ceiling. 
